  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Team members who trust each other communicate openly and honestly, collaborate effectively, and support each other. The goal is to create an environment at work where people feel safe, comfortable, open to being themselves, and supported by one another. \n\nStart by reading a short article, [Rebuilding Companies as Communities](https://hbr.org/2009/07/rebuilding-companies-as-communities).\n\nThen ask yourself:\n\n> Do we have strong connections on our team?\n\n> Could we build a stronger community among us?\n\n> What can I do personally to build a stronger sense of community on the team?\n\n### What does \"community\u00e2\u20ac\u009d mean to your team?\n\nAsk each team member what community means to them and to suggest three ideas toward building a stronger sense of community. Review as a team and pick one to carry out. Revisit the list with your team over time to continue strengthening the sense of community.",
